@startuml
title Spock example: worker fixtures and specification state
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
hide footbox

participant "Spock specifications\nin one worker JVM" as specs
participant "TestInfrastructure\nlazy worker holder" as fixture
database "Worker-local\nPostgreSQL" as postgres
queue "Worker-local\nRabbitMQ" as rabbit

note over specs,rabbit
  ShardPilot selects whole specification families before execution.
  SpockConfig disables feature/iteration parallelism inside the worker.
end note

specs -> fixture : Spec A setupSpec(): allocate database
group First access only: Startables.deepStart(...).join()
  par PostgreSQL startup
    fixture -> postgres : Start with random mapped endpoint
    postgres --> fixture : Ready
  else RabbitMQ startup
    fixture -> rabbit : Start with random mapped endpoints
    rabbit --> fixture : Ready
  end
end
fixture -> postgres : CREATE DATABASE example_<generated A>
fixture --> specs : Store URL in Spec A @Shared field

loop Spec A features / data-table iterations
  specs -> postgres : Fresh JDBC connection; isolated rows/tables
  specs -> rabbit : AMQP when required: private client / queue
  specs -> specs : Close clients; assert captured results
end

specs -> fixture : Spec B setupSpec(): allocate database
fixture -> postgres : CREATE DATABASE example_<generated B>
fixture --> specs : Spec B @Shared URL; reuse same service pair

note over specs,rabbit
  No cleanupSpec() container stop or Testcontainers extension ownership.
  Every iteration stays on its specification's owner shard.
end note

specs -> specs : Worker exits after all selected specifications
note over postgres,rabbit
  Ryuk removes the disposable containers on worker exit.
  Another shard / worker owns an independent fixture pair.
end note
@enduml
